The reviewer's integrated disposition clears everything in #9272 at `804b4681cb` except the one item already in progress. It covered:
- production semantics and canonical parity;
- the merge and its receipts;
- the reverse-gap pin and its qualified claim about the existing sorts;
- the six saved result arrays, which match exactly;
- the qualified wording around CPU and the reverse-gap statement.

It also read the real-store replay directly. The reason-first plan switched to fact-first with keyed probes, 0.568 ms down to 0.005 ms. With no statistics, the plan was already fact-first. So the cause is confirmed, and that's also exactly why the empty-store test can't catch a reversion.

**The only open item** is the discriminating `wanted_hosts` test the implementer is writing now. When it hands back, I'll send both reviewers the frozen test-only change with its focused receipt, and the revert-and-fail log. No broad rerun was requested. Then #9272 can be marked ready.
